IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 5 Division 3, ss 184A to 184G -- passing resolutions by written means, and resolutions of one-member companies.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Percentages are tested by integer comparison (100 times the part against the percentage times the whole).
-- Sections 76(9B)(e), 175A(1)(a) and 183 belong to other clusters: whether a resolution is one of those is an input, or the answer of the other cluster's function.

§ `Section 184A(1), (2) and (9): who may pass resolutions by written means`

-- (9): "In this section and sections 184B to 184F, 'unlisted public company' means a public company the securities of which are not listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities
-- exchange outside Singapore."
-- src:16759 | (9) In this section and sections 184B to 184F, “unlisted public
-- src:16760 | company” means a public company the securities of which are not
-- src:16761 | listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore
-- src:16762 | or any securities exchange outside Singapore.
@ref s 184A(9) (src:16759-16762)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its securities are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184A(9) the company is an unlisted public company` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` AND (NOT `its securities are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): ""unlisted public company" means a public company the securities of which are not listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore" (a "means" definition)

-- (1): "Despite any other provision of this Act, a private company or an unlisted public company may pass any resolution by written means in accordance with this section and sections 184B to 184F."
-- (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a resolution mentioned in section 175A(1)(a) or a resolution for which special notice is required." A company outside the two kinds is outside the grant (NOTHING, scope limit); an excepted resolution is a flat negative (JUST FALSE).
-- src:16640 | 184A.—(1) Despite any other provision of this Act, a private
-- src:16641 | company or an unlisted public company may pass any resolution by
-- src:16642 | written means in accordance with the provisions of this section and
-- src:16643 | sections 184B to 184F.
-- src:16647 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a resolution mentioned in
-- src:16648 | section 175A(1)(a) or a resolution for which special notice is
-- src:16649 | required.
@ref s 184A(1) and (2) (src:16640-16649)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is an unlisted public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is one mentioned in section 175A(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `special notice is required of the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184A(1) the company may pass the resolution by written means` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company is a private company` OR `the company is an unlisted public company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a private company or an unlisted public company may pass any resolution by written means" (a scope limit with no "only"; periods ruling (c))
    ELSE (IF `the resolution is one mentioned in section 175A(1)(a)` OR `special notice is required of the resolution`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a resolution mentioned in section 175A(1)(a) or a resolution for which special notice is required" (a flat negative; N2)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- The phrase "a private company or an unlisted public company" recurs in s 184A(1), s 184B(1), s 184D(1), s 184E(1) and s 184F(1); the function below answers it from the three facts a person states
-- (private, public, listed), so that a seat question does not combine them itself.
-- src:16640 | 184A.—(1) Despite any other provision of this Act, a private
-- src:16641 | company or an unlisted public company may pass any resolution by
-- src:16642 | written means in accordance with the provisions of this section and
-- src:16643 | sections 184B to 184F.
@ref s 184A(1) (src:16640-16643)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its securities are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 184A(1) the company is a private company or an unlisted public company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 184A(9) the company is an unlisted public company` `the company is a public company` `its securities are listed for quotation or quoted on an approved exchange in Singapore or any securities exchange outside Singapore`
    WHEN JUST unlisted THEN (`the company is a private company` OR unlisted)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the company is a private company`

§ `Section 184A(3) to (5): when a resolution is passed by written means`

-- (3): "A special resolution is passed by written means if the resolution indicates that it is a special resolution and if it has been formally agreed on any date by one or more members of the company who on that date
-- represent -- (a) at least 75%; or (b) if the constitution of the company requires a greater majority for that resolution, that greater majority, of the total voting rights of all the members who on that date would have the
-- right to vote on that resolution at a general meeting of the company." "if" read as the definition (marginal reading (a), F-15).
-- src:16656 | (3) A special resolution is passed by written means if the resolution
-- src:16657 | indicates that it is a special resolution and if it has been formally
-- src:16658 | agreed on any date by one or more members of the company who on
-- src:16659 | that date represent —
-- src:16661 | (a) at least 75%; or
-- src:16663 | (b) if the constitution of the company requires a greater
-- src:16664 | majority for that resolution, that greater majority,
-- src:16666 | of the total voting rights of all the members who on that date would
-- src:16667 | have the right to vote on that resolution at a general meeting of the
-- src:16668 | company.
@ref s 184A(3) (src:16656-16668)
GIVEN `the resolution indicates that it is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the voting rights of the members who have formally agreed` IS A NUMBER
      `the total voting rights of all the members who would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage of the total voting rights the constitution requires, if it requires a greater majority than 75%` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184A(3) the special resolution is passed by written means` MEANS
    LET required MEANS
        CONSIDER `the percentage of the total voting rights the constitution requires, if it requires a greater majority than 75%`
        WHEN JUST greater THEN (IF greater GREATER THAN 75 THEN greater ELSE 75)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN 75
    IN IF    `the resolution indicates that it is a special resolution`
         AND `the total voting rights of all the members who would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting` GREATER THAN 0
         AND 100 TIMES `the voting rights of the members who have formally agreed` AT LEAST required TIMES `the total voting rights of all the members who would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting`
       THEN JUST TRUE
       ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A special resolution is passed by written means if the resolution indicates that it is a special resolution and if it has been formally agreed ... by one or more members ... who ... represent -- (a) at least 75%; or (b) ... that greater majority" (an "if" definition read as no when failed; marginal reading (a); F-15)

-- (4): "An ordinary resolution is passed by written means if the resolution does not indicate that it is a special resolution and if it has been formally agreed ... by one or more members ... who ... represent -- (a) a majority; or
-- (b) if the constitution of the company requires a greater majority for that resolution, that greater majority". A majority is more than half; a greater majority the constitution requires is met by that percentage (F-44).
-- src:16672 | (4) An ordinary resolution is passed by written means if the
-- src:16673 | resolution does not indicate that it is a special resolution and if it has
-- src:16674 | been formally agreed on any date by one or more members of the
-- src:16675 | company who on that date represent —
-- src:16677 | (a) a majority; or
-- src:16679 | (b) if the constitution of the company requires a greater
-- src:16680 | majority for that resolution, that greater majority,
-- src:16682 | of the total voting rights of all the members who on that date would
-- src:16683 | have the right to vote on that resolution at a general meeting of the
-- src:16684 | company.
@ref s 184A(4) (src:16672-16684)
GIVEN `the voting rights of the members who have formally agreed` IS A NUMBER
      `the total voting rights of all the members who would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage of the total voting rights the constitution requires, if it requires a greater majority than a majority` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 184A(4) the formal agreements represent the majority the subsection requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the percentage of the total voting rights the constitution requires, if it requires a greater majority than a majority`
    WHEN JUST greater THEN
        (IF greater GREATER THAN 50
         THEN 100 TIMES `the voting rights of the members who have formally agreed` AT LEAST greater TIMES `the total voting rights of all the members who would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting`
         ELSE 2 TIMES `the voting rights of the members who have formally agreed` GREATER THAN `the total voting rights of all the members who would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 2 TIMES `the voting rights of the members who have formally agreed` GREATER THAN `the total voting rights of all the members who would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting`

@ref s 184A(4) (src:16672-16684)
GIVEN `the resolution indicates that it is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the voting rights of the members who have formally agreed` IS A NUMBER
      `the total voting rights of all the members who would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage of the total voting rights the constitution requires, if it requires a greater majority than a majority` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184A(4) the ordinary resolution is passed by written means` MEANS
    IF    (NOT `the resolution indicates that it is a special resolution`)
      AND `the total voting rights of all the members who would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting` GREATER THAN 0
      AND `s 184A(4) the formal agreements represent the majority the subsection requires` `the voting rights of the members who have formally agreed` `the total voting rights of all the members who would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting` `the percentage of the total voting rights the constitution requires, if it requires a greater majority than a majority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An ordinary resolution is passed by written means if the resolution does not indicate that it is a special resolution and if it has been formally agreed ... by one or more members ... who ... represent -- (a) a majority; or (b) ... that greater majority" (an "if" definition read as no when failed; marginal reading (a); F-15, F-44)

-- src:16688 | (4A) A resolution mentioned in section 76(9B)(e) is passed by
-- src:16689 | written means if the resolution indicates that it is a resolution
-- src:16690 | mentioned in that provision and if it has been formally agreed on any
-- src:16691 | date by all the members of the company who on that date would have
-- src:16692 | the right to vote on that resolution at a general meeting of the
-- src:16693 | company.
@ref s 184A(4A) (src:16688-16693)
GIVEN `the resolution indicates that it is a resolution mentioned in section 76(9B)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the members who on that date would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting have formally agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184A(4A) the resolution mentioned in section 76(9B)(e) is passed by written means` MEANS
    IF `the resolution indicates that it is a resolution mentioned in section 76(9B)(e)` AND `all the members who on that date would have the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting have formally agreed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A resolution mentioned in section 76(9B)(e) is passed by written means if the resolution indicates that it is a resolution mentioned in that provision and if it has been formally agreed ... by all the members" (an "if" definition read as no when failed; marginal reading (a); F-15)

-- (5): "a resolution of a company is formally agreed by a member if -- (a) the company receives from the member (or the member's proxy if this is allowed) a document that -- (i) is given to the company in legible form or a permitted
-- alternative form; (ii) indicates the member's agreement ... by way of the member's signature (or the member's proxy's signature if that is allowed), or such other method as the constitution may provide; and (iii) includes the text of
-- the resolution or otherwise makes clear that it is that resolution that is being agreed to; and (b) the member (or the member's proxy) had a legible text of the resolution before giving that document."
-- src:16695 | (5) For the purposes of this section, a resolution of a company is
-- src:16696 | formally agreed by a member if —
-- src:16698 | (a) the company receives from the member (or the member’s
-- src:16699 | proxy if this is allowed) a document that —
-- src:16701 | (i) is given to the company in legible form or a
-- src:16702 | permitted alternative form;
-- src:16707 | (ii) indicates the member’s agreement (or agreement on
-- src:16708 | the member’s behalf) to the resolution by way of the
-- src:16709 | member’s signature (or the member’s proxy’s
-- src:16710 | signature if that is allowed), or such other method
-- src:16711 | as the constitution may provide; and
-- src:16713 | (iii) includes the text of the resolution or otherwise makes
-- src:16714 | clear that it is that resolution that is being agreed to;
-- src:16715 | and
-- src:16717 | (b) the member (or the member’s proxy) had a legible text of
-- src:16718 | the resolution before giving that document.
@ref s 184A(5) (src:16695-16718)
GIVEN `the company receives from the member, or the member's proxy if that is allowed, a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is given to the company in legible form or a permitted alternative form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document indicates the member's agreement by signature, or by such other method as the constitution may provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document includes the text of the resolution or otherwise makes clear that it is that resolution that is being agreed to` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member, or the member's proxy, had a legible text of the resolution before giving the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184A(5) the resolution is formally agreed by the member` MEANS
    IF    `the company receives from the member, or the member's proxy if that is allowed, a document`
      AND `the document is given to the company in legible form or a permitted alternative form`
      AND `the document indicates the member's agreement by signature, or by such other method as the constitution may provide`
      AND `the document includes the text of the resolution or otherwise makes clear that it is that resolution that is being agreed to`
      AND `the member, or the member's proxy, had a legible text of the resolution before giving the document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a resolution of a company is formally agreed by a member if -- (a) the company receives ... a document that -- (i) ...; (ii) ...; and (iii) ...; and (b) the member ... had a legible text of the resolution before giving that document" (an "if" definition read as no when failed; marginal reading (a); F-15)

-- src:16722 | (6) Nothing in subsection (3), (4) or (4A) is to be construed as
-- src:16723 | requiring the requisite number of members to formally agree to the
-- src:16724 | resolution on a single day.
@ref s 184A(6) (src:16722-16724)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184A(6) subsection (3), (4) or (4A) requires the requisite number of members to formally agree to the resolution on a single day` MEANS
    JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in subsection (3), (4) or (4A) is to be construed as requiring the requisite number of members to formally agree to the resolution on a single day" (a flat negative; N2)

-- src:16726 | (6A) For the purposes of this section, something is “in legible form
-- src:16727 | or a permitted alternative form” if, and only if, it is sent or otherwise
-- src:16728 | supplied —
-- src:16730 | (a) in a form (such as a paper document) that is legible before
-- src:16731 | being sent or otherwise supplied and does not change form
-- src:16732 | during that process; or
-- src:16734 | (b) in another form that —
-- src:16736 | (i) is currently agreed between the company and the
-- src:16737 | person as a form in which the thing may be sent or
-- src:16738 | otherwise supplied to the company; and
-- src:16740 | (ii) is such that documents sent or supplied in that form
-- src:16741 | can (where particular conditions are met) be received
-- src:16742 | in legible form or be made legible following receipt
-- src:16743 | in non‑legible form.
@ref s 184A(6A) (src:16726-16743)
GIVEN `the thing is legible before being sent or otherwise supplied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing does not change form during that process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form is currently agreed between the company and the person as a form in which the thing may be sent or otherwise supplied to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `documents sent or supplied in that form can be received in legible form or be made legible following receipt in non-legible form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184A(6A) the thing is in legible form or a permitted alternative form` MEANS
    IF    (`the thing is legible before being sent or otherwise supplied` AND `the thing does not change form during that process`)
       OR (`the form is currently agreed between the company and the person as a form in which the thing may be sent or otherwise supplied to the company` AND `documents sent or supplied in that form can be received in legible form or be made legible following receipt in non-legible form`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "something is 'in legible form or a permitted alternative form' if, and only if, it is sent or otherwise supplied -- (a) ...; or (b) ..." (an "if, and only if" definition)

-- src:16745 | (7) Any reference in this Act or any other law to the passing or
-- src:16746 | making of a resolution, or the passing or making of a resolution at a
-- src:16747 | meeting, includes a reference to the passing of the resolution by
-- src:16748 | written means in accordance with this section.
@ref s 184A(7) (src:16745-16748)
GIVEN `the resolution is passed by written means in accordance with section 184A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184A(7) the reference to the passing or making of a resolution includes its passing by written means` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is passed by written means in accordance with section 184A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Any reference in this Act or any other law to the passing or making of a resolution ... includes a reference to the passing of the resolution by written means in accordance with this section" (a list that is not closed)

-- src:16750 | (8) Any reference in this Act or any other law to the doing of
-- src:16751 | anything at a general meeting of a company includes a reference to
-- src:16756 | the passing of a resolution authorising the doing of that thing by
-- src:16757 | written means in accordance with this section.
@ref s 184A(8) (src:16750-16757)
GIVEN `a resolution authorising the doing of the thing is passed by written means in accordance with section 184A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184A(8) the reference to the doing of a thing at a general meeting includes the passing of a resolution authorising it by written means` MEANS
    IF `a resolution authorising the doing of the thing is passed by written means in accordance with section 184A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Any reference in this Act or any other law to the doing of anything at a general meeting of a company includes a reference to the passing of a resolution authorising the doing of that thing by written means in accordance with this section" (a list that is not closed)

§ `Section 184B: the requirements for passing a resolution by written means`

-- (1): "A resolution of a private company or an unlisted public company may only be passed by written means if -- (a) either -- (i) agreement to the resolution was first sought by the directors of the company in accordance with
-- section 184C; or (ii) a requisition for that resolution was first given to the company in accordance with section 183 and, by reason of that notice, the documents referred to in section 183(3A) in respect of the resolution were
-- served on members of the company in accordance with section 183(3A); (b) the constitution of the company does not prohibit the passing of resolutions (either generally or for the purpose in question) by written means; and
-- (c) all conditions in the company's constitution relating to the passing of the resolution by written means are met." "only if" closes the gate: JUST FALSE when it is not met.
-- src:16768 | 184B.—(1) A resolution of a private company or an unlisted public
-- src:16769 | company may only be passed by written means if —
-- src:16771 | (a) either —
-- src:16773 | (i) agreement to the resolution was first sought by the
-- src:16774 | directors of the company in accordance with
-- src:16775 | section 184C; or
-- src:16777 | (ii) a requisition for that resolution was first given to the
-- src:16778 | company in accordance with section 183 and, by
-- src:16779 | reason of that notice, the documents referred to in
-- src:16780 | section 183(3A) in respect of the resolution were
-- src:16781 | served on members of the company in accordance
-- src:16782 | with section 183(3A);
-- src:16784 | (b) the constitution of the company does not prohibit the
-- src:16785 | passing of resolutions (either generally or for the purpose
-- src:16786 | in question) by written means; and
-- src:16788 | (c) all conditions in the company’s constitution relating to the
-- src:16789 | passing of the resolution by written means are met.
@ref s 184B(1) (src:16768-16789)
GIVEN `the company is a private company or an unlisted public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `agreement to the resolution was first sought by the directors in accordance with section 184C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a requisition for the resolution was first given in accordance with section 183 and the documents referred to in section 183(3A) were served on members in accordance with that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution prohibits the passing of resolutions by written means, either generally or for the purpose in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all conditions in the constitution relating to the passing of the resolution by written means are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184B(1) the resolution may be passed by written means` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a private company or an unlisted public company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A resolution of a private company or an unlisted public company may only be passed by written means if" (the subsection speaks of those two kinds of company; a scope limit)
    ELSE (IF    (`agreement to the resolution was first sought by the directors in accordance with section 184C` OR `a requisition for the resolution was first given in accordance with section 183 and the documents referred to in section 183(3A) were served on members in accordance with that subsection`)
             AND (NOT `the constitution prohibits the passing of resolutions by written means, either generally or for the purpose in question`)
             AND `all conditions in the constitution relating to the passing of the resolution by written means are met`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only be passed by written means if -- (a) either -- (i) ...; or (ii) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ..." (an "only if" list)

-- src:16793 | (2) Any resolution that is passed in contravention of subsection (1)
-- src:16794 | is invalid.
@ref s 184B(2) (src:16793-16794)
GIVEN `the resolution was passed by written means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184B(2) the resolution is invalid because it was passed in contravention of subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the resolution was passed by written means`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of "any resolution that is passed in contravention of subsection (1)"
    ELSE (IF `the answer under subsection (1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE (IF `the answer under subsection (1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question): the resolution was passed in accordance with subsection (1), so this subsection does not make it invalid
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (1) gave no answer, so the text does not say whether there was a contravention

§ `Section 184C: where the directors seek agreement`

-- src:16798 | 184C.—(1) The directors of a private company or an unlisted
-- src:16799 | public company who wish to seek agreement to a resolution of the
-- src:16800 | company and for it to be passed by written means must send to each
-- src:16805 | member, having the right to vote on that resolution at a general
-- src:16806 | meeting, a copy of the text of the resolution.
@ref s 184C(1) (src:16798-16806)
GIVEN `the directors wish to seek agreement to a resolution and for it to be passed by written means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have sent each member having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting a copy of the text of the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184C(1) the directors have sent each member entitled to vote a copy of the text of the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the directors wish to seek agreement to a resolution and for it to be passed by written means` AND `the directors have sent each member having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting a copy of the text of the resolution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors of a private company or an unlisted public company who wish to seek agreement to a resolution ... and for it to be passed by written means must send to each member, having the right to vote on that resolution at a general meeting, a copy of the text of the resolution" (a duty's own question)

-- (2): "As far as practicable, the directors must comply with subsection (1) as respects every member at the same time and without delay." No number of days: "without delay" is an input (F-40).
-- src:16810 | (2) As far as practicable, the directors must comply with
-- src:16811 | subsection (1) as respects every member at the same time and
-- src:16812 | without delay.
@ref s 184C(2) (src:16810-16812)
GIVEN `the directors complied with subsection (1) as respects every member at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors complied with subsection (1) without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was practicable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184C(2) the directors have complied with subsection (1) as respects every member at the same time and without delay` MEANS
    IF `the directors complied with subsection (1) as respects every member at the same time` AND `the directors complied with subsection (1) without delay`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE (IF `it was practicable to do so`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "As far as practicable, the directors must comply with subsection (1) as respects every member at the same time and without delay" (a duty's own question; it was practicable)
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "As far as practicable" -- where it was not practicable the text does not say what the directors must do instead

-- src:16814 | (3) Without limiting any other means of complying with
-- src:16815 | subsections (1) and (2), the directors have complied with those
-- src:16816 | subsections if they secure that the same paper document containing
-- src:16817 | the text of the resolution is sent without delay to each member in turn.
@ref s 184C(3) (src:16814-16817)
GIVEN `the directors secure that the same paper document containing the text of the resolution is sent without delay to each member in turn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184C(3) the directors have complied with subsections (1) and (2)` MEANS
    IF `the directors secure that the same paper document containing the text of the resolution is sent without delay to each member in turn`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Without limiting any other means of complying with subsections (1) and (2), the directors have complied with those subsections if they secure that ..." (one means among others; the list is not closed)

-- src:16819 | (4) Subject to section 184D, if the resolution is passed before the
-- src:16820 | directors have complied with subsection (1) as respects every
-- src:16821 | member, that fact does not affect the validity of the resolution or
-- src:16822 | any obligation already incurred by the directors under subsections (1)
-- src:16823 | and (2).
@ref s 184C(4) (src:16819-16823)
GIVEN `the resolution is passed before the directors have complied with subsection (1) as respects every member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 184D applies to the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184C(4) the validity of the resolution is not affected by its being passed before the directors complied with subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `section 184D applies to the resolution`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to section 184D" -- section 184D governs where it applies
    ELSE (IF `the resolution is passed before the directors have complied with subsection (1) as respects every member`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of a resolution passed before the directors have complied

§ `Section 184D: members may require a general meeting`

-- (1): "Any member or members of a private company or an unlisted public company representing at least 5% of the total voting rights of all the members having the right to vote on a resolution at a general meeting of the company
-- may, within 7 days after -- (a) the text of the resolution has been sent ... in accordance with section 184C; or (b) the documents referred to in section 183(3A) ... have been served ..., as the case may be, give notice to the
-- company requiring that a general meeting be convened for that resolution." Outside the 7 days is JUST FALSE (a period the text fixes, ruling (a)); a holding under 5% is outside the grant (NOTHING, scope limit).
-- src:16827 | 184D.—(1) Any member or members of a private company or an
-- src:16828 | unlisted public company representing at least 5% of the total voting
-- src:16829 | rights of all the members having the right to vote on a resolution at a
-- src:16830 | general meeting of the company may, within 7 days after —
-- src:16832 | (a) the text of the resolution has been sent to the member or
-- src:16833 | members in accordance with section 184C; or
-- src:16835 | (b) the documents referred to in section 183(3A) in respect of
-- src:16836 | the resolution have been served on the member or
-- src:16837 | members,
-- src:16839 | as the case may be, give notice to the company requiring that a
-- src:16840 | general meeting be convened for that resolution.
@ref s 184D(1) (src:16827-16840)
GIVEN `the company is a private company or an unlisted public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the voting rights the member or members represent` IS A NUMBER
      `the total voting rights of all the members having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the text of the resolution was sent to them in accordance with section 184C or the documents referred to in section 183(3A) were served on them` IS A DATE
      `the day they gave notice to the company requiring a general meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184D(1) the member or members may give notice requiring a general meeting to be convened for the resolution` MEANS
    IF    `the company is a private company or an unlisted public company`
      AND `the total voting rights of all the members having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting` GREATER THAN 0
      AND 100 TIMES `the voting rights the member or members represent` AT LEAST 5 TIMES `the total voting rights of all the members having the right to vote on the resolution at a general meeting`
    THEN (IF `period: the date is within a period after` `the day the text of the resolution was sent to them in accordance with section 184C or the documents referred to in section 183(3A) were served on them` `the day they gave notice to the company requiring a general meeting` 7 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, within 7 days after -- (a) the text of the resolution has been sent ...; or (b) the documents ... have been served" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling (a))
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any member or members of a private company or an unlisted public company representing at least 5% of the total voting rights" (a scope limit with no "only"; periods ruling (c))

-- (2): "Where notice is given under subsection (1) -- (a) the resolution is invalid even though it may have in the meantime been passed in accordance with section 184A; and (b) the directors must proceed to convene a general
-- meeting for the resolution." A "where" gate: JUST FALSE when no notice was given (periods ruling (b)).
-- src:16844 | (2) Where notice is given under subsection (1) —
-- src:16846 | (a) the resolution is invalid even though it may have in the
-- src:16847 | meantime been passed in accordance with section 184A;
-- src:16848 | and
-- src:16850 | (b) the directors must proceed to convene a general meeting
-- src:16851 | for the resolution.
@ref s 184D(2) (src:16844-16851)
GIVEN `notice is given under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184D(2)(a) the resolution is invalid because notice was given under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `notice is given under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where notice is given under subsection (1) -- (a) the resolution is invalid even though it may have in the meantime been passed in accordance with section 184A" (a "where" gate on a flat statement)

@ref s 184D(2) (src:16844-16851)
GIVEN `notice is given under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have proceeded to convene a general meeting for the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184D(2)(b) the directors have proceeded to convene a general meeting for the resolution` MEANS
    IF `notice is given under subsection (1)` AND `the directors have proceeded to convene a general meeting for the resolution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where notice is given under subsection (1) -- ... (b) the directors must proceed to convene a general meeting for the resolution" (a duty's own question; "proceed" has no time limit)

§ `Section 184DA: the period for agreeing to a written resolution`

-- (1): "Unless the constitution of a private company or an unlisted public company otherwise provides, a resolution proposed to be passed by written means lapses if it is not passed before the end of the period of 28 days
-- beginning with the date on which the written resolution is circulated to the members of the company." The period is counted by the keel's P10 (the day of circulation is day 1).
-- src:16858 | 184DA.—(1) Unless the constitution of a private company or an
-- src:16859 | unlisted public company otherwise provides, a resolution proposed to
-- src:16860 | be passed by written means lapses if it is not passed before the end of
-- src:16861 | the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the written
-- src:16862 | resolution is circulated to the members of the company.
@ref s 184DA(1) (src:16858-16862)
GIVEN `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 184DA(1) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date of circulation` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members` 28 Days

GIVEN `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members` IS A DATE
      `the day the resolution was passed, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 184DA(1) the resolution was passed before the end of the period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the resolution was passed, if it has been`
    WHEN JUST passed THEN passed AT MOST `s 184DA(1) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date of circulation` `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

@ref s 184DA(1) (src:16858-16862)
GIVEN `the constitution otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members` IS A DATE
      `the day the resolution was passed, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184DA(1) the resolution has lapsed` MEANS
    IF `the constitution otherwise provides`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Unless the constitution ... otherwise provides" -- the constitution governs
    ELSE (IF `s 184DA(1) the resolution was passed before the end of the period` `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members` `the day the resolution was passed, if it has been`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "lapses if it is not passed before the end of the period" -- it was passed within the period
          ELSE (IF `the date asked` GREATER THAN `s 184DA(1) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date of circulation` `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "lapses if it is not passed before the end of the period of 28 days" -- the period has not yet ended on the date asked

-- src:16868 | (2) The agreement to a resolution is ineffective if indicated after the
-- src:16869 | expiry of that period.
@ref s 184DA(2) (src:16868-16869)
GIVEN `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members` IS A DATE
      `the day the agreement was indicated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184DA(2) the agreement to the resolution is ineffective` MEANS
    IF `the day the agreement was indicated` GREATER THAN `s 184DA(1) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date of circulation` `the date the written resolution is circulated to the members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The agreement to a resolution is ineffective if indicated after the expiry of that period" (an "if" gate read as no when failed; marginal reading (a); F-15)

§ `Section 184E: the company's duty to notify members`

-- src:16876 | 184E.—(1) Where a resolution of a private company or an unlisted
-- src:16877 | public company is passed by written means, the company must —
-- src:16879 | (a) notify every member that it has been passed; and
-- src:16881 | (b) do so within 15 days from the earliest date on which a
-- src:16882 | director or secretary of the company is aware that it has
-- src:16883 | been passed.
@ref s 184E(1) (src:16876-16883)
GIVEN `the resolution of a private company or an unlisted public company is passed by written means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earliest date on which a director or secretary of the company is aware that it has been passed` IS A DATE
      `the date the company had notified every member that it has been passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184E(1) the company has notified every member that the resolution has been passed in time` MEANS
    IF NOT `the resolution of a private company or an unlisted public company is passed by written means`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a resolution of a private company or an unlisted public company is passed by written means, the company must" (a "where" gate on a duty)
    ELSE (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the earliest date on which a director or secretary of the company is aware that it has been passed` `the date the company had notified every member that it has been passed` 15 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must -- (a) notify every member that it has been passed; and (b) do so within 15 days from the earliest date on which a director or secretary of the company is aware that it has been passed" (a duty's own question; a period the text fixes)

GIVEN `the earliest date on which a director or secretary of the company is aware that it has been passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 184E(1) the number of days from the awareness to the last day for notifying members` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the earliest date on which a director or secretary of the company is aware that it has been passed` 15 Days) MINUS `the earliest date on which a director or secretary of the company is aware that it has been passed`

-- src:16887 | (2) Non‑compliance with this section does not render the resolution
-- src:16888 | invalid.
@ref s 184E(2) (src:16887-16888)
GIVEN `the company did not comply with section 184E` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184E(2) the resolution is invalid because the company did not comply with section 184E` MEANS
    IF `the company did not comply with section 184E`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Non-compliance with this section does not render the resolution invalid" (a flat negative; N2)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of non-compliance with the section

§ `Section 184F: recording resolutions passed by written means`

-- (1): "Where a resolution of a private company or an unlisted public company is passed by written means, the company must cause a record of the resolution, and the indication of each member's agreement ..., to be entered in a book
-- in the same way as minutes of proceedings of a general meeting of the company." No time limit is stated, so no trace can show it breached.
-- src:16892 | 184F.—(1) Where a resolution of a private company or an unlisted
-- src:16893 | public company is passed by written means, the company must cause
-- src:16894 | a record of the resolution, and the indication of each member’s
-- src:16895 | agreement (or agreement on the member’s behalf) to it, to be entered
-- src:16896 | in a book in the same way as minutes of proceedings of a general
-- src:16897 | meeting of the company.
@ref s 184F(1) (src:16892-16897)
GIVEN `the resolution of a private company or an unlisted public company is passed by written means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has caused a record of the resolution and of each member's agreement to be entered in a book in the same way as minutes of proceedings of a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184F(1) the company has caused the record to be entered in a book` MEANS
    IF `the resolution of a private company or an unlisted public company is passed by written means` AND `the company has caused a record of the resolution and of each member's agreement to be entered in a book in the same way as minutes of proceedings of a general meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a resolution ... is passed by written means, the company must cause a record of the resolution ... to be entered in a book" (a duty's own question; a "where" gate)

-- src:16901 | (2) Non‑compliance with subsection (1) does not render the
-- src:16902 | resolution invalid.
@ref s 184F(2) (src:16901-16902)
GIVEN `the company did not comply with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184F(2) the resolution is invalid because the company did not comply with subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the company did not comply with subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Non-compliance with subsection (1) does not render the resolution invalid" (a flat negative; N2)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of non-compliance with subsection (1)

-- src:16907 | (3) Any such record, if purporting to be signed by a director or the
-- src:16908 | secretary of the company, is evidence of the proceedings in passing
-- src:16909 | the resolution.
@ref s 184F(3) (src:16907-16909)
GIVEN `the record purports to be signed by a director or the secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184F(3) the record is evidence of the proceedings in passing the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the record purports to be signed by a director or the secretary of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any such record, if purporting to be signed by a director or the secretary of the company, is evidence of the proceedings in passing the resolution" (an evidence rule whose "if" gate failed)

-- src:16911 | (4) Where a record is made in accordance with this section, then,
-- src:16912 | until the contrary is proved, the requirements of this Act with respect
-- src:16913 | to those proceedings are deemed to have been complied with.
@ref s 184F(4) (src:16911-16913)
GIVEN `a record is made in accordance with section 184F` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184F(4) the requirements of this Act with respect to the proceedings are deemed to have been complied with` MEANS
    IF NOT `a record is made in accordance with section 184F`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a record is made in accordance with this section, then, until the contrary is proved, the requirements of this Act with respect to those proceedings are deemed to have been complied with" (a "where" gate on a deeming)
    ELSE (IF `the contrary is proved`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the contrary is proved" -- the period the text fixes has ended (periods ruling (a); delegated-defences ruling item (d), an "until" bar)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:16915 | (5) Section 189 applies in relation to a record made in accordance
-- src:16916 | with this section as it applies in relation to minutes of proceedings of a
-- src:16917 | general meeting.
@ref s 184F(5) (src:16915-16917)
GIVEN `a record is made in accordance with section 184F` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184F(5) section 189 applies to the record as it applies to minutes of proceedings of a general meeting` MEANS
    IF `a record is made in accordance with section 184F`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 189 applies in relation to a record made in accordance with this section" -- a record not so made is outside the subsection

§ `Section 184G: resolutions of one-member companies`

-- src:16921 | 184G.—(1) Despite anything in this Act, a company that has only
-- src:16922 | one member may pass a resolution by the member recording the
-- src:16923 | resolution and signing the record.
@ref s 184G(1) (src:16921-16923)
GIVEN `the company has only one member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member records the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member signs the record` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184G(1) the company may pass the resolution by the member recording it and signing the record` MEANS
    IF `the company has only one member` AND `the member records the resolution` AND `the member signs the record`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Despite anything in this Act, a company that has only one member may pass a resolution by the member recording the resolution and signing the record" (a grant whose condition failed, or a company outside the subsection)

-- src:16925 | (2) If this Act requires information or a document relating to the
-- src:16926 | resolution to be lodged with the Registrar, that requirement is
-- src:16927 | satisfied by lodging the information or document with the resolution
-- src:16928 | that is passed.
@ref s 184G(2) (src:16925-16928)
GIVEN `this Act requires information or a document relating to the resolution to be lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information or document is lodged with the resolution that is passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184G(2) the requirement to lodge the information or document is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `this Act requires information or a document relating to the resolution to be lodged with the Registrar` AND `the information or document is lodged with the resolution that is passed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that requirement is satisfied by lodging the information or document with the resolution that is passed" (one way to satisfy it; the text does not say that no other way does)

§ `Regulative rules of ss 184C, 184D, 184E and 184F`

DECLARE `s 184 written act` IS ONE OF
    `s 184C(1) send each member a copy of the text of the resolution`
    `s 184D(2)(b) proceed to convene a general meeting for the resolution`
    `s 184E(1) notify every member that the resolution has been passed`
    `s 184F(1) enter the record of the resolution in a book`

-- s 184C(1): "without delay" is no number of days, so there is no clock to miss (no breach path; F-40).
-- src:16798 | 184C.—(1) The directors of a private company or an unlisted
-- src:16799 | public company who wish to seek agreement to a resolution of the
-- src:16800 | company and for it to be passed by written means must send to each
-- src:16805 | member, having the right to vote on that resolution at a general
-- src:16806 | meeting, a copy of the text of the resolution.
@ref s 184C(1) (src:16798-16806)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 184 written act`
`s 184C(1) the directors must send each member a copy of the text of the resolution (no time limit)` MEANS
    PARTY `Board of directors` `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 184C(1) send each member a copy of the text of the resolution`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 184C(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `Board of directors` `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the directors did not send each member a copy of the text of the resolution" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- s 184D(2)(b): "must proceed to convene" states no time limit and no consequence.
-- src:16844 | (2) Where notice is given under subsection (1) —
-- src:16846 | (a) the resolution is invalid even though it may have in the
-- src:16847 | meantime been passed in accordance with section 184A;
-- src:16848 | and
-- src:16850 | (b) the directors must proceed to convene a general meeting
-- src:16851 | for the resolution.
@ref s 184D(2) (src:16844-16851)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 184 written act`
`s 184D(2)(b) the directors must proceed to convene a general meeting for the resolution (no time limit)` MEANS
    PARTY `Board of directors` `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 184D(2)(b) proceed to convene a general meeting for the resolution`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 184D(2)(b) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `Board of directors` `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the directors did not proceed to convene a general meeting for the resolution" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- s 184E(1): time 0 is the earliest day a director or secretary is aware that the resolution has been passed; the last day is 15 days later.
-- src:16876 | 184E.—(1) Where a resolution of a private company or an unlisted
-- src:16877 | public company is passed by written means, the company must —
-- src:16879 | (a) notify every member that it has been passed; and
-- src:16881 | (b) do so within 15 days from the earliest date on which a
-- src:16882 | director or secretary of the company is aware that it has
-- src:16883 | been passed.
@ref s 184E(1) (src:16876-16883)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 184 written act`
`s 184E(1) the company must notify every member that the resolution has been passed within 15 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 184E(1) notify every member that the resolution has been passed`
    WITHIN 15
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not notify every member that the resolution had been passed within 15 days from the earliest date on which a director or secretary of the company was aware that it had been passed"

-- s 184F(1): no time limit and no consequence is stated.
-- src:16892 | 184F.—(1) Where a resolution of a private company or an unlisted
-- src:16893 | public company is passed by written means, the company must cause
-- src:16894 | a record of the resolution, and the indication of each member’s
-- src:16895 | agreement (or agreement on the member’s behalf) to it, to be entered
-- src:16896 | in a book in the same way as minutes of proceedings of a general
-- src:16897 | meeting of the company.
@ref s 184F(1) (src:16892-16897)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 184 written act`
`s 184F(1) the company must cause the record of the resolution to be entered in a book (no time limit)` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 184F(1) enter the record of the resolution in a book`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 184F(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not cause the record of the resolution to be entered in a book" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
